Short:        Full-screen media centre for the Amiga
Author:       Brian King
Uploader:     Brian King
Type:         util/wb
Version:      [VERSION]
Requires:     68020+, Kickstart 3.1+; mpega.library, flacdec.library
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1.0

AmigaMCE is a fast, full-screen media centre for the Amiga, in the spirit
of Kodi and Windows Media Center: games and demos from Amiga Game Selector
(AGS), tracker music, internet radio, the music and photos on your Plex
server and your pictures, all in one place, driven by keyboard, mouse or
joystick.

Copy the AmigaMCE drawer anywhere and double-click it. On an Amiga Game
Selector 3 installation it is a drop-in companion: AGS's games and demos,
its modules and its pictures are found by themselves. On any other Amiga,
Settings > Folders says where your music, modules and pictures are.
Everything plays inside AmigaMCE, on its own screen and the Amiga's own
sound.


Features
--------
Games and demos
- Browses the AGS menu tree (Games, Demos, Disk Magazines, Favourites) by
  category, never as one giant flat list. On screens 640 or more wide the
  selected title's screenshot and fact sheet sit in a pane beside it.
- Launches titles through their AGS .run scripts, honouring the AGS
  Expert, ExpertPerm and Adult settings. While a game runs AmigaMCE frees
  everything it can, and comes back on the same entry afterwards.
- Long lists (All Games, menus split A-Z) are kept in an index in the
  Cache drawer, so they open at once; only letters that changed are read
  again. Deleting the Cache drawer is always safe. Screenshots and fact
  sheets are read by a second process, so the list never waits for disk.

Mods
- Modules from the MODS: assign and up to eight folders chosen in
  Settings > Folders > Modules, and on AGS from ST-00:Modules,
  ST-00:C64Music and AGS:Mods (its menu music). ProTracker modules play on AmigaMCE's own replayer, after the
  ProTracker 2.3D play routine and timed by a CIA timer. Hundreds of other
  formats (OctaMED, TFMX, Future Composer, Hippel, AHX, SID...) play
  through EaglePlayer's and DeliTracker's players where they are
  installed (AGS has them). 6- and 8-channel MODs play on the same
  replayer, channels 5 to 8 mixed onto Paula's four the way ProTracker
  4.1 does (its mixer, by Andreas Wendorf). XM, S3M, IT, MTM and 669
  are mixed by modplug.library on a 68020 or better. Packed modules
  (PowerPacker, XPK...) are unpacked with xfdmaster.library.

Radio
- Internet radio from radio-browser.info: top voted, most listened to,
  trending, chiptune, demoscene, by genre or by country (A to Z, your own
  country first, from your Locale settings). Only stations an Amiga can
  play are listed: MP3, working, and no higher in bitrate than this Amiga
  copes with. Now Playing shows the song titles the station sends.
- With AmiSSL 5 and Settings > Networking > HTTPS on, stations that
  stream over HTTPS are listed and play too, marked HTTPS in the lists
  and on Now Playing.

Music (Plex)
- The music libraries of a Plex Media Server on your network: by artist,
  album or recently added, with covers and details beside the list.
- Plex converts each track to an MP3 this Amiga can decode: 22 kHz mono
  on a 68020/030, 24 kHz stereo on a 68040/060, at a higher bitrate on a
  fast one. On a fast Amiga with flacdec.library, MP3 and FLAC tracks
  play as stored. Plain HTTP on your own network: no AmiSSL needed.
- Servers are found on the network by Plex's own discovery (GDM). With
  AmiSSL 5, sign in at plex.tv by a code entered at plex.tv/link on a
  phone or computer: no token to copy, and your account's servers are
  listed too.

Music (files)
- MP3, FLAC, WAV, AIFF and 8SVX files on this Amiga, under Music beside
  Plex: the MUSIC: assign, if there is one, and up to eight folders chosen
  in Settings > Folders > Music. Only folders with music somewhere
  inside are listed (in a folder of more than 64 folders, all of them).
  Fire plays a file with the rest of its folder as
  the playlist, with seeking. FLAC needs flacdec.library; a 68020/030
  plays it in mono at about 22 kHz.
- Beside the list: the file's title, artist, album and year (ID3 tags,
  FLAC's comments, AIFF and 8SVX names), its format and length, and its
  cover: the folder's cover file (cover, folder or front .png or .jpg) or
  the picture inside the file. Now Playing shows them too.
- A beets library (beets.io) with its database in MUSIC: (musiclibrary.db
  or library.db) adds Music library (beets): Artists, Albums and Recently
  added, then an artist's albums and an album's tracks, without reading
  the folders (quick on a network share). The database is only ever read,
  through AmigaMCE's own Libs/amcesql.library (SQLite). Its albums are
  read once, a few seconds on an 030, and kept in Cache until the
  database changes. Tracks in WMA, AAC or other formats AmigaMCE does
  not play are left out, as are file names with characters Latin-1 lacks.

Now Playing
- Title, artist, album and cover, a level meter per channel (labelled for
  modules by their samples), a position bar you can click to seek, and
  buttons for previous, back, play/pause, stop, forward, next, loop
  (again at its end, until turned off) and volume.
- The music plays on while you browse; the lists you came from mark what
  is playing, and a Now playing row at their top brings you back to it.
- Stop gives Paula and its timer back to the system, so other programs
  can play sound.

Pictures
- Browses the PICTURES: assign, up to eight folders chosen in Settings >
  Folders > Pictures and AGS's Media:Images, with a preview of the picture
  or folder selected,
  shows pictures full screen on AmigaMCE's own screen (no mode switch) and
  plays folders as slideshows, in the pictures' own colours where the
  screen allows. Pictures are decoded by the installed datatypes.
  Moving the mouse shows the pointer and buttons for the previous
  picture, the slideshow (play or pause) and the next.
- Plex photos: the photo libraries of your Plex server at the top of
  Pictures, albums and photos with a preview beside the list, full
  screen and as slideshows. The server makes each photo the size of the
  screen (PNG, JPEG above 640x512); the next is fetched while one is
  shown, and a slideshow waits for a slow one rather than skip it.

Videos
- IFF ANIMs from the VIDEOS: assign, up to eight folders chosen in
  Settings > Folders > Videos and AGS's Media:Animations, with a frame
  of each beside the list (a later one when it starts blank), its size,
  colours, frame count and length. Each plays on a screen in its own
  display mode (HAM, extra halfbrite, interlace, overscan) as it was
  made, read from the file a frame at a time, so the biggest play too:
  ANIM-5, 7 and 8. Its own sound plays in step with the pictures, by
  AHI if that is the sound output, else Paula; what was playing waits
  (a station or a track is stopped, and goes on afterwards).
- Moving the mouse brings up controls over the picture: from the start,
  play/pause, stop, loop, volume (when it has sound), the time and the
  length; a click on the line of how far it has got goes there. Up/Down
  set the volume; Esc or the right button stops. At its end it goes
  back to its first frame and waits there, unless loop is on.
- In a Workbench window it is made as large as the window holds,
  larger or smaller; the full-screen button shows it on the whole
  display, on a screen in Workbench's own mode (no mode switch), and
  back.
- MPEG video on a ZZ9000: .mpg, .mpeg, .vob and transport streams
  (.ts, .m2ts), MPEG-1 or MPEG-2, decoded by the card and shown on its
  overlay, its sound (MPEG audio or AC-3) played as music is. Without
  one, MPEG-1 is decoded by the CPU on RTG screens.
- DVDs: while a DVD-Video disc is in a drive, its volume is at the top
  of Videos with a disc beside it. Fire plays its film, or its
  programmes one after another (a disc of episodes); N and P, or the
  controls' |<< and >>|, the previous and next chapter or programme. Of
  its sound tracks, the one the card is likeliest to play. Needs a
  ZZ9000 and Libs/amcedvd.library (in the archive); no menus yet, and
  no encrypted (CSS) discs.

Screens
- 320x200/256 lowres, 640x200/256 hires and 640x400/512 laced on OCS, ECS
  and AGA; 640x480, 800x600 and 1024x768 on RTG, or Automatic: the
  graphics card when the Workbench is on it (the largest of those sizes
  that fits the Workbench's screen), else hires on AGA, lowres before it.
- Japanese, Chinese and Korean names (from Plex, stations and song
  tags) are shown in their own characters, at 12 or 15 pixels (without
  Fonts/amce-cjk, as [JP], [KO] or [CJK]). Greek names too, in the smooth
  style's own letters or at 12 pixels.
- Laced screens choose their pixel font (Galmuri or Pixelify Sans); big
  RTG screens scale the layout up, in a pixel look or a smooth,
  anti-aliased one. Never uses Extra Half-Brite.
- Or a window on Workbench, when Workbench is on a graphics card at 15
  bits or more: Settings > Display > Workbench window, the icon's WINDOWED
  tooltype (shipped as (WINDOWED): take the brackets away), or
  AmigaMCE WINDOWED from a Shell; a choice made in Settings comes first.
  Its text is Small, Medium or Large (512 x 384, 640 x 480 or 800 x 600
  at first, as far as Workbench has room); in the pixel style the font
  is the size. Resize it (its grip, bottom right) and the layout
  follows, the text staying its size; it opens again where and as large
  as it was left. Its Project menu (the right button over its title
  bar): About, Settings, Full screen, Iconify, Quit. Iconify (Amiga-I,
  or the title bar's gadget on OS 3.2; full screen too) leaves an
  AppIcon on Workbench and the music playing: double-click it to come
  back; Workbench's Tools > Quit AmigaMCE quits. Its zoom gadget swaps
  it for a mini player (the cover, what plays, the time, the buttons,
  mute, the volume, a meter; 1x, 2x or 3x by Workbench's size); its own
  zoom gadget, a click on the cover, Esc or Return bring the window
  back. Pictures and videos go full
  screen from it (their button, F or Amiga-F) on a screen in
  Workbench's own mode, so the monitor does not change mode.
- The menu folds to its icons while you browse, giving the lists and
  Now Playing its room, and opens again with the focus or the pointer on
  it; it slides open and shut where the Amiga draws it quickly.
- Flicker-free scrolling lists and text pages. A long list always shows
  a scroll bar (how long it is, and where you are in it), which the mouse
  can drag or click.


Requirements
------------
- Kickstart 3.1 or later and a 68020 or better, on OCS, ECS, AGA or RTG.
- Amiga Game Selector 3 for Games and Demos (found through AGS:).
- For Radio and Plex: a running TCP/IP stack (bsdsocket.library).
- For MP3: mpega.library (the installer offers it). For FLAC:
  flacdec.library (Aminet: util/libs/flacdec; on a 68060 its 68060 build).
- Optional: EaglePlayer's players (Aminet: mus/play/Eagleplayer, with its
  own installer, which assigns Eagleplayer2:; AGS has them) or
  DeliTracker's, modplug.library and
  xfdmaster.library for more module formats (the installer offers the
  two libraries); picture datatypes; AHI for sound through a sound card;
  AmiSSL 5 for HTTPS (secure radio stations, signing in at plex.tv).


Installation
------------
Double-click Install-AmigaMCE: it asks where AmigaMCE should go and which
languages to install, your Workbench's ticked, and keeps the settings of
an earlier installation. Not on AGS (which has them), it then offers
modplug.library, mpega.library and xfdmaster.library from Aminet, ticked
where LIBS: has none or an older one; a newer one is never replaced. Or copy the AmigaMCE drawer to your hard drive
yourself (all its languages come along), keeping its Fonts drawer next to
the program.

On AGS, if it boots straight into its own menu, quit AGS to Workbench
first, then double-click AmigaMCE.

Languages
---------
English, Deutsch, Français, Italiano, Español, Svenska, Suomi, Dansk,
Norsk, Nederlands, Português, Japanese, Greek and Korean. AmigaMCE
speaks your Workbench's language (Locale prefs) when its catalog is
installed;
Settings > General > Language chooses another. Workbench 3.x has no
Japanese or Korean locale, so they are only ever chosen there: AmigaMCE
draws them with its own glyphs (Fonts/amce-cjk), needing nothing from
the system. Greek is drawn with AmigaMCE's own glyphs too, so it needs no
Greek fonts or ReplaceTopaz; it is chosen by itself where Locale prefs
put Greek first. The translations are new: corrections are
welcome (catalogs/*.ct in the source, FlexCat's format).


Controls
--------
  Up/Down      move (held: faster)   Shift+Up/Down  page
  Fire/Return  play a game, module, station or track; open a folder
  Right        open a folder; on a game, its details
  Left/Esc     back                  Esc at menu    press twice to quit
  A-Z          jump to letter        Right mouse    back
  Mouse        one click opens a folder or setting; a game or picture is
               selected by one click and played by two. The path above a
               list (Games > All Games...) links back to each level
  Mouse wheel  scroll                Scroll bar     click to page, drag
  CD32 pad     shoulder buttons: next / previous letter

  Pictures     Fire views a picture or plays a folder marked with the
               play arrow as a slideshow. In the viewer, Left/Right
               previous/next, Fire or Space slideshow on/off, Esc back.
  Videos       Fire plays an animation. Playing: Space, Fire or a click
               pause; Up/Down or the wheel volume; Esc, Blue or the right
               button stop; the mouse moved shows the controls.
  Now Playing  Left/Right choose a button, Fire presses it; Space
               play/pause; S stop; N/P next/previous; , and . back and
               forward; Up/Down or the wheel volume; a click on the bar
               jumps there; V, or the cycle gadget at the meters' top
               right, the level meters or the spectrum (the playing
               marker in the header and lists follows it; greyed where
               the music allows the meters only, as under MHI). Opened
               from another section (a module's page from Music), its
               title says where the music is from: a click there, or G,
               goes to that folder; Esc goes back where you were. Esc goes back, the
               music playing on.


Settings
--------
  General      Language, Debug
  Display      Window (full screen or a Workbench window, where Workbench
               can take one), Screen mode (full screen) or Text size (a
               window), Style (a laced or RTG screen: the font, those
               whose layout fits; RTG: or Smooth), Double buffering
               (RTG), Visualisation
               (Now Playing's level meters, or HippoPlayer's spectrum
               analyser; under MHI the meters), Jump scrolling (very
               long lists step a letter at a time)
  Sound        Paula, or AHI (16-bit) for radio, Plex and music files;
               MP3 by mpega.library or an MHI driver (which decodes
               and plays it itself); FLAC by flacdec.library
  Folders      Where Music, Mods, Pictures and Videos find their files:
               the MUSIC:, MODS:, PICTURES: and VIDEOS: assigns on or
               off, folders added (Add a folder...) or taken out (Fire
               twice); AGS's own drawers are found by themselves
  Networking   HTTPS: secure connections, with AmiSSL 5 (radio stations,
                 signing in at plex.tv)
               Radio: the highest bitrate listed, which
                 radio-browser.info server the lists come from
               Plex: on or off, the server, signing in at plex.tv,
                 lower quality audio
               Stream buffer: short, normal or long
               Network interface: which one connections go out from

Settings are saved in ENVARC:AmigaMCE/. If a screen mode does not suit
your display, delete ENVARC:AmigaMCE/ScreenMode to go back to Automatic.

Debug shows the CPU load and memory use in the header and writes a timing
log to AmigaMCE.log next to the program (RAM:AmigaMCE.log if that drawer
is read-only).


Setting up Plex
---------------
1. Settings > Networking > Plex: turn Plex on, then choose your server
   under Plex server (servers on the network are found for you).
2. If the server asks for a sign-in: with AmiSSL 5 installed, turn on
   Settings > Networking > HTTPS, then choose Settings > Networking >
   Plex > Sign in at plex.tv and enter the code it shows at plex.tv/link
   on a phone or computer. Your account's servers then appear under Plex
   server. Without AmiSSL, set your Plex token from the Shell:
     SetEnv SAVE AmigaMCE/PlexToken <token>
   About > Plex in AmigaMCE says where to find it.
3. Your music libraries appear under Music, photo libraries at the top
   of Pictures.


Not there yet
-------------
- DVD menus and subtitles; encrypted (CSS) discs.
- MPEG video on AGA screens without a ZZ9000.
- Modules play on Paula only; AHI for them comes later.


History
-------
0.8.9  Videos plays MPEG: on a ZZ9000 (MPEG-1 and MPEG-2, program and
       transport streams, with their sound), and MPEG-1 by the CPU on
       RTG screens without one. DVDs in a drive: their film, or their
       programmes one after another, chapters by N and P and the
       controls, the sound track the card plays best
       (Libs/amcedvd.library: libdvdread and libdvdnav). The CPU's
       pictures go on the graphics card's YUV overlay where there is one
       (Settings > Display: Use overlay when available), decoded about
       twice as fast (2.6 times on a 68020), its B pictures passed over
       while it is behind. One set of
       control glyphs for Now playing, the mini player, ANIMs, videos
       and DVDs, square on lowres, hires and laced screens alike.
0.8.8  MP3 seeks land on a real frame (no error after a sound output
       change). The volume kept between runs. MHI at the level of mpega
       through Paula or AHI. On Workbench, the smooth style leaves pens
       free for other programs. A MED song EaglePlayer's MED players turn
       down goes to the mixer without every other player asked first.
       The mini player's meters across.
0.8.5  Iconify: the window's gadget on OS 3.2, Project > Iconify or
       Amiga-I (full screen too) leave an AppIcon with a musical note on
       Workbench, the music playing on; double-clicked, AmigaMCE is back
       where it was. Workbench's Tools menu quits it meanwhile. A mini
       player on the window's zoom gadget. Mute on Now playing (M). Sound
       output changed in Settings applies to what plays at once. JPEGs
       no datatype takes (a camera's, from Plex) read by AmigaMCE.
0.8.1  Now playing at the top of every section's lists, its label in
       orange; what was playing at quit back at the next start, stopped,
       Play going on from where it was. MED songs (MED_note): their
       length and seeking, real levels on the meters, the right tempo
       where the player gives none, four tracks on Paula's four. AHI:
       its default mode (the Music unit's); mpega at its best quality on
       a fast Amiga. Viewer: Previous's arrow, no transition when stepped
       by hand, the bar kept clear of one. The window: Amiga-F and a
       double-click on its title bar for full screen; Display's two-way
       choices as checkboxes. Plex tokens kept out of the log.
0.8.0  Slideshow transitions (Settings > Display): Off, Fade, Cross-fade,
       Tiles or Wipe; on a screen with a colour table, a fade. Korean.
       The window follows Workbench's screen mode changing, back into a
       window when it can. Videos resized as they play. Note players
       (MED_note) mixed on a 68020 or better: samples of any length, its
       periods read right, 5-8 channels. Icons highlighted with images
       of their own; the drawer's a GlowIcon.
0.7.2  A window on Workbench (15-bit or deeper, on a graphics card):
       Settings > Display > Workbench window, the icon's WINDOWED tooltype or
       WINDOWED from a Shell; text Small, Medium or Large; resized by its
       grip, the layout and text pages following; its Project menu; the
       tips bar going once seen with the mouse; its place and size kept.
       Pictures and videos full screen from it on a screen in
       Workbench's own mode (no mode switch). The viewer: the pointer and
       previous, play/pause, next and full-screen buttons with the mouse.
       Videos: made to fit a window, larger or smaller, at any depth; at
       their end back to the first frame, stopped; a click on their
       progress line seeks. Loop, on Now Playing and video's controls.
       EaglePlayer: a module's kind from what it holds, note players
       (MED_note) heard, and a player whose check hangs left out.
0.7.1  Music: beets libraries in MUSIC: browsed by artist and album;
       music folders with the spinner while read. HTTPS by AmiSSL 5
       (Settings > Networking): secure radio stations play, and Plex
       signs in at plex.tv by a code (plex.tv/link), the account's
       servers listed with their own tokens. Radio: titles in time with
       the music, smoother over MHI, Now playing in its lists. 6- and
       8-channel MODs on AmigaMCE's own replayer, mixed onto Paula (after
       ProTracker 4.1's mixer). ZZ9000: found, and MP3 decoded on the
       card. JPEG thumbnails decoded by AmigaMCE itself (jdec), faster
       than a datatype. Greek. Lists: the scroll bar always, the letter
       over the rows, tags kept while scrolling; the menu stays open until
       a list is gone into; a joystick for Games.
0.7.0  Videos: IFF ANIMs (ANIM-5, 7 and 8) from Media:Animations, VIDEOS:
       and Videos folders, played on a screen in their own mode (HAM,
       extra halfbrite, interlace, overscan) a frame at a time from the
       file, their sound in step (AHI or Paula) while what played waits,
       with controls over the picture when the mouse moves; a frame of
       each beside the list. The menu folds to its icons on every screen,
       sliding where drawing is quick, and stays open while the pointer is
       in it. Settings > Screen is now Display, with Jump scrolling.
       amcesql.library for reading beets libraries later. Faster Plex
       slideshows; smoother hover highlights; coasting kept short.
0.6.0  Plex photo libraries in Pictures: browsing, viewing, slideshows.
       AHI output and MHI MP3 decoding for radio, Plex and music files.
       Music files: MP3, FLAC, WAV, AIFF and 8SVX from the MUSIC:
       assign and Music folders, with tags and covers; FLAC from Plex
       as stored (flacdec.library); 68020+. Japanese, Chinese and
       Korean names in their own characters. In eleven languages besides
       English (Japanese among them), with an installer.
       HippoPlayer's spectrum analyser on Now
       Playing (V, or Settings > Screen > Visualisation). Settings >
       Folders: the music, modules and pictures of an Amiga without AGS
       (MUSIC:, MODS:, PICTURES: and up to eight folders each). Screen
       mode Automatic follows a Workbench on a graphics card; RTG
       screens choose their pixel font. Long lists brake for their end
       and coast on when let go at speed.
0.5.0  Music from a Plex Media Server; Settings in pages (General,
       Screen, Sound, Networking); radio bitrate limit, list server and
       stream buffer settings; network interface choice; Countries A to Z
       with your own first; Now Playing seeking, covers and new buttons.


